I don't know how you get to ascend multiple times without developing
the following instinct: if you enter a room and encounter banding
monsters that aren't complete pushovers, backtrack to the exit you
already were in. Your chances of encountering something on the way
back are very low, and your chance of getting surrounded by the other
monsters is zero, unless they're faster than you. Of course, you
should also check your inventory *before* you get in trouble. And
consider whether prayer might be a better option than reading an
unID'd scroll. There are, after all, only three scrolls that could
really help you in the described situation (and I'm not sure that
scare monster will work against non-Elbereth-respecting creatures,
either). (And don't forget to check if you've already identified any/
all of those!)

Of course, if you were already in the room, then heading to the
nearest exit makes sense, assuming you can't tell where the monsters
are coming from. But you should explore dark rooms with your back to
the wall, (a) to minimize the amount of surrounding that is possible,
and (b) to actually map the room.

